  "retained_failures": [
    "Initial pilot removed isolbox recognition and extracted no isolation device; restoring recognition exposed the unconnected NWell terminal. Private physical-overlap/contact connections fix both.",
    "Early contacts violated active area and contact spacing. Corrected actual layout and retained native failures without altering rule thresholds.",
    "Initial full matrix used a 3.6 um outer square that failed nmosi.b/c. Replaced the positive with the derived 4.06 um contact boundary; 4.05 um remains an explicit rejection.",
    "Early mixed fixture crossed signal exits with ring metal and used undersized gate/contact landings. Corrected those fixture routes and retained unchanged transistor channel/tap dimensions.",
    "Mixed pilot lost the child tap recognition, collapsing its body into the source net. The product fix preserves the annotation; final native output retains all three devices.",
    "One test harness expected Cnt.a rather than the actual CntB.a and looked in diagnostics rather than findings. Its native DRC failure was correct; the harness now demands the exact native rule.",
    "The first Windows receipt harness searched silicon instead of physical-flow; completed native results are retained. The final five-case staging/receipt harness passes.",
    "Initial evidence archive listing included Python assets twice. A fresh deduplicated archive verifies all objects; native check results were unaffected."
  ],
